# Reading: Sharps and Dotted Rhythms (repertoire plan: st-read-first-sharps). An original reading
# study in first position (finger 1 on fret 1, finger 2 on fret 2 ...), 16 bars of 4/4:
#   bars 1-8 in D major (F# and C#): C# at string 2 fret 2 and at string 5 fret 4;
#   bars 9-16 in A major (F#, C# and G#): G# at string 3 fret 1.
# Each half is two 4-bar phrases with a long-short dotted rhythm (dotted quarter, eighth). A tie
# carries a note across the bar line in bars 3-4 (E over A7 into D) and bars 11-12 (B over E7
# into A); the tied note is held, not picked again. The teacher strums the chords.
title: Reading: Sharps and Dotted Rhythms
